        <body>
            <div xml:id="d437">

                <pb facs="0520" n="354" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg354"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.00/1064</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Gonzales </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-12T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 12, 1917—5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your February 10, 10 p.m. and February 11, 11 p.m. Department has made public
                    this afternoon statement transmitted in its February 10, 7 p.m. You are
                    authorized to give it to Cuban press. If President Menocal and Zayas have no
                    objections you are authorized to send military attaché to Santa Clara to observe
                    elections but to give no counsel and take no active part in supervision.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
